        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Right, that is what I think it might be helpful, boolean option that can be passed as part of the config table on the initial setup, i.e.\n``` lua\n{\n  palette = palette,\n  italic = true,\n  bold = true\n}\n```\nAnd that might change some of the highlight group to use italic/bold. For example comments could use italic text, and maybe keyword can use bold. I'm not expert (actually not even noob), but I just think at least to me that it might help to further differentiate some different groups specially for developers.\n\nI would be happy to look into the code and make the changes myself but just wondering if this is of any interest and aligned with the design of this plugin. ",
            "created_at": "2025-12-23T20:23:12Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2191#issuecomment-3687880301",
