        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> And that might change some of the highlight group to use italic/bold. For example comments could use italic text, and maybe keyword can use bold. I'm not expert (actually not even noob), but I just think at least to me that it might help to further differentiate some different groups specially for developers.\n\nOkay, I see. Unfortunately, I think this is out of scope for 'mini.base16' as it is primarily designed to follow original [Base16 design system](https://github.com/chriskempson/base16). So this kind of customization feels a bit too much.\n\nMy best suggestion is to manually adjust some highlight groups after `require('mini.base16').setup()`. For example:\n\n```lua\nlocal p = {\n  -- Define your palette here\n}\nrequire('mini.base16').setup({ palette = p })\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'Comment', { fg = p.base03, italic = true })\n```",
            "created_at": "2025-12-23T20:35:34Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/2191#issuecomment-3687903876",
